  "term": "inverse kinematics",
  "definition": "Inverse kinematics is the mathematical process of working backward from a desired platform position and orientation to calculate the required movements or lengths of its mechanical parts. In this source, it refers to computing the rod displacements needed for a flexible Stewart platform to reach a target pose with high precision.",
